/*
 *
 * Aggregates all class declarations representing function prototypes.
 *
 * The prototype subsystem defines the various forms of callable signatures
 * manipulated by the generator: basic function prototypes, named prototypes,
 * method prototypes, lambda prototypes, constructors, and destructors. These
 * values describe the structure of a callable entity (parameters, mutability,
 * return type, etc.) without representing an actual invocation.
 *
 * This module provides a flat and stable public entry point for all prototype
 * representations, while each specific prototype form is implemented in its own
 * dedicated submodule.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::prototypes
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/prototypes.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2025-01-04
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
